    <GaugingStation location="Sandon Bridge" name="Sandon Brook" number="37013">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Insensitive 'Essex' profile weir gauging a rural catchment with reservoirs affecting the regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Insensitive. One peak flow rating applied across period of record. Modular limit around 0.6m. All but highest flows contained. The flow is derived through the rating curve and then under non-modular conditions, a macro is applied within WISKI which applies a reduction factor. Therefore, under high flows, the stage and flow won't match through the modular rating. Subject to weed growth and siltation, particularly downstream.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">'Essex' profile (modified Flat V Crump) weir with crest tapping.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">No POT data are presented for this station as they have no non-modular flow correction applied. AMAX data have been corrected. Some float-run gaugings are thought to be unreliable. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Reservoir(s) in catchment affect runoff. Naturalised flows (1963-1976) account for reservoir compensation water (0.011 cumecs) and storm overflows. Minor additions from industrial effluent.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Catchment area includes 13.7 sq km draining to Hanningfield Reservoir 10km upstream. London Clay with sand and gravel over high ground in northeast, Boulder Clay in south. Rural, mainly arable land with some grassland.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">SRE</Comment>
        </Comments>
